[154.341367, "i", "cat > ../failed_reasons.txt <<EOF\nThe build fails because the modules (common, factory, service, value) are inheriting from 'auto-parent' version 3, which seems to have a dependency on 'tools.jar' at a system path that does not exist in the current Java 11 environment. The error message explicitly states it cannot find 'tools.jar' at '/usr/lib/jvm/java-11-openjdk-amd64/../lib/tools.jar'.\n\nThe project root contains a newer 'auto-parent' version 4-SNAPSHOT which is being built but not used by the modules. This newer parent likely has better handling for tools.jar or can be modified.\n\nPlan:\n1. Update 'common/pom.xml', 'factory/pom.xml', 'service/pom.xml', and 'value/pom.xml' to inherit from 'auto-parent' version 4-SNAPSHOT.\n2. Add <relativePath>../pom.xml</relativePath> to the parent declaration in these files so they find the local parent.\nEOF\n"]
[154.344081, "o", "cat > ../failed_reasons.txt <<EOF\r\n> The build fails because the modules (common, factory, service, value) are inheriting from 'auto-parent' version 3, which seems to have a dependency on 'tools.jar' at a system path that does not exist in the current Java 11 environment. The error message explicitly states it cannot find 'tools.jar' at '/usr/lib/jvm/java-11-openjdk-amd64/../lib/tools.jar'.\r\n> \r\n> The project root contains a newer 'auto-parent' version 4-SNAPSHOT which is being built but not used by the modules. This newer parent likely has better handling for tools.jar or can be modified.\r\n> \r\n> Plan:\r\n> 1. Update 'common/pom.xml', 'factory/pom.xml', 'service/pom.xml', and 'value/pom.xml' to inherit from 'auto-parent' version 4-SNAPSHOT.\r\n> 2. Add <relativePath>../pom.xml</relativePath> to the parent declaration in these files so they find the local parent.\r\n> EOF\r\nroot@74feeeadfed3:/home/travis/build/failed/google/auto# "]
